:EDATA.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKTIMZON.Work with Time Zone Descriptions - Help
:P.The time zone descriptions in library QSYS. A description gives the
offset of standard time from UTC, the names of standard and daylight
saving time and when daylight saving time starts and ends. The system
value QTIMZON names the description the system's local time follows;
it is marked with a greater-than sign. F11 shows the daylight saving
names, the alternate names and the text in turn.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKTIMZON/OPTIONS'.Options
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Prompts CHGTIMZON for the description.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Deletes the description with DLTTIMZON. The description QTIMZON
names cannot be deleted.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Shows everything the description holds.
:PT.6=Print
:PD.Writes the description's details to a spooled file.
:PT.8=Update system value
:PD.Makes the description the system's time zone (QTIMZON). Local time
changes at once.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKTIMZON/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to a description and press Enter.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPTZ.Display Time Zone Description Details - Help
:P.Everything a time zone description holds: its offset, the names of
standard and daylight saving time with the messages they come from, the
rule that starts and ends daylight saving time, the year offset, the
alternate name and the text.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NOW'.Date and time
:P.The current local date and time and the abbreviation of the time in
force.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OFFSET'.Offset
:P.The difference between standard time in the zone and UTC, in hours and
minutes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MARK'.Current zone
:P.A greater-than sign marks the description the system value QTIMZON
names.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TIMZON'.Time zone
:P.The name of the time zone description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ABBR'.Standard time abbreviation
:P.The short name of standard time in the zone.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FULL'.Standard time name
:P.The full name of standard time in the zone.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DABBR'.Daylight saving time abbreviation
:P.The short name of daylight saving time; blank when the zone keeps
none.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DFULL'.Daylight saving time name
:P.The full name of daylight saving time.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALT'.Alternate name
:P.Another name for the zone, such as its name in the IANA time zone
database.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TEXT'.Text
:P.The description's text.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSG'.Message
:P.The message the names come from, when the description takes them from
a message file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGF'.Message file
:P.The message file of the messages and its library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/EDGE'.Daylight saving time start and end
:P.The month, the day of the week, which of those days in the month and
the local time daylight saving time starts or ends at.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SHIFT'.Daylight saving time shift
:P.How many minutes the clock moves forward when daylight saving time
starts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/YEAROFS'.Year offset
:P.The number of years added to the Gregorian year when dates of the
zone are shown.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRK'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the list again with the current descriptions.
:PT.F6=Create
:PD.Prompts CRTTIMZON to create a description.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line.
:PT.F11=Display another view
:PD.Shows the daylight saving names, the alternate names, the text or
the standard names, in turn.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Shows the start of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Shows the end of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DTL'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
